==File Formats==
===Arena===
Arena uses <code>.dat</code> files to store font information. [[Arena:Files#Misc_Utilities|ArenaFont within ArenaSuite]] is a good tool to view and edit.
===Daggerfall===
Daggerfall uses <code>.fnt</code> files to store font information, but not like the conventional use of the format. Daggerfall Font Editor is a good tool to view and edit the fonts.
===Morrowind===
Morrowind uses <code>.tex</code> and <code>.fnt</code> files to store font information. The <code>.tex</code> image file stores all of the characters, while the <code>.fnt</code>file—unconventionally—stores the position, size, and other various information of each character in the image. FontReader is a good tool to view and save the fonts.

===Oblivion===
Similarly to Morrowind, Oblivion uses <code>.tex</code> and <code>.fnt</code> files within [[Oblivion Mod:BSA File Format|<code>Oblivion - Misc.bsa</code>]] to store font information. The <code>.tex</code> image file stores all of the characters, while the <code>.fnt</code> file—unconventionally—stores the position, size, and other various information of each character in the image. Bethesda Archive Extractor is a good tool to open the <code>.bsa</code>, and Oblivion Font Editor is a good tool to view and save the fonts.

===Skyrim===
Skyrim's fonts are compiled within <code>.swf</code>s within [[Skyrim Mod:Archive File Format|<code>Skyrim - Interface.bsa</code>]]. Bethesda Archive Extractor is a good tool to open the <code>.bsa</code> and JPEXS is a good tool to decompile an <code>.swf</code> and export a font as a <code>.ttf</code>.

